WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.898
The sun rose as it did every other day, promising light and warmth,

2
00:00:04.898 --> 00:00:10.430
but today, no amount of sunshine could brighten the March sisters' darkened hearts.

3
00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:20.313
While Meg and Jo, who had not slept a wink all night, watched for any signs of change in Beth's condition, they talked about what to do with Amy.

4
00:00:20.314 --> 00:00:23.786
"Obviously she can't stay here," stated Meg.

5
00:00:23.786 --> 00:00:28.156
"Maybe Mr. Laurence and Laurie can look after her," suggested Jo.

6
00:00:28.156 --> 00:00:31.775
"That wouldn't be proper," Meg said, shaking her head.

7
00:00:31.776 --> 00:00:36.760
"Besides, they've done so much for us already we couldn't burden them with anything more."

8
00:00:36.761 --> 00:00:44.967
At the same moment the sisters thought of their only other solution, but both of them were hesitant to say it until finally Meg said,

9
00:00:44.968 --> 00:00:48.111
"We are left with no other choice but . . . "

10
00:00:48.112 --> 00:00:55.360
"Yes, Aunt March's," sighed Jo, finishing Meg's words and already feeling sorry for Amy.

11
00:00:55.361 --> 00:01:00.114
"If you can talk with Aunt March, then I'll break the news to Amy," said Meg.

12
00:01:00.114 --> 00:01:08.604
As the girls were agreeing to the plan, Dr. Bangs, looking as though he hadn't had much sleep as well, returned to check up on Beth.

13
00:01:08.605 --> 00:01:15.479
Again, the kind doctor told Meg and Jo that he was concerned about them, and that they must look after themselves first

14
00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:18.254
in order to be better caregivers to Beth.

15
00:01:18.255 --> 00:01:23.992
Leaving Dr. Bangs to tend to Beth, Meg and Jo closed the door firmly behind them.

16
00:01:23.993 --> 00:01:29.913
"We'd better go and talk to Amy," said Meg, holding out her hand for the key to the bedroom.

17
00:01:29.913 --> 00:01:36.616
Although it was cruel to lock Amy up, it was the only way they could keep her away from Beth.

18
00:01:36.617 --> 00:01:42.312
Having unlocked the door, Meg and Jo expected Amy to come flying at them in a fit.

19
00:01:42.313 --> 00:01:50.809
However, they found her eerily quiet as she sat on the floor, hugging her knees close, her eyes swollen from crying.

20
00:01:50.809 --> 00:01:54.268
"Is Beth dead?" was Amy's first question.

21
00:01:54.268 --> 00:02:02.670
Although she did not know the details, Amy was extremely shrewd and could sense the seriousness of Beth's illness without being told.

22
00:02:02.671 --> 00:02:09.413
Meg squatted down beside her and said in a motherly voice, "It's all right. Everything is going to be fine."

23
00:02:09.414 --> 00:02:18.264
"Dr. Bangs is with her now. She's stable for the time being, but there hasn't been any improvement in her condition," Jo said truthfully.

24
00:02:18.265 --> 00:02:25.212
"Beth has scarlet fever and that means you mustn't be in the house or else you will catch it too," said Meg.

25
00:02:25.212 --> 00:02:28.344
"But where will I go?" asked Amy.

26
00:02:28.345 --> 00:02:33.112
"You need to go and stay with Aunt March," Meg said carefully.

27
00:02:33.113 --> 00:02:43.467
After two seconds of stunned silence, Amy replied: "No! I won't stay with that old lady. She gives me the creeps!"

28
00:02:43.468 --> 00:02:48.868
"Amy!" Meg said sharply, "You must never speak about our relative in that manner.

29
00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:52.096
And you have no say in the matter, I'm sorry to say.

30
00:02:52.097 --> 00:02:55.733
Pack a few things, please, and get ready to leave immediately."

31
00:02:55.734 --> 00:03:04.567
Amy argued, begged, cried, and shouted, but in the end, she saw her sisters' decision was firm.

32
00:03:04.568 --> 00:03:11.632
After a wearisome visit with Aunt March where Jo had to endure criticism of her parents and their upbringing of the girls,

33
00:03:11.633 --> 00:03:15.662
Jo's relative finally agreed to allow Amy to stay with her.

34
00:03:15.663 --> 00:03:23.391
Laurie, on the other hand, proved his loyalty as a friend once again by wholeheartedly offering to do whatever he could to help.

35
00:03:23.392 --> 00:03:27.348
"Laurie, can't I stay with you and your grandfather?"

36
00:03:27.349 --> 00:03:31.765
Amy asked him as the Laurence carriage was taking them to Aunt March's.

37
00:03:31.766 --> 00:03:39.751
"I wish you could, Amy," Laurie answered, "but your sisters have made up their minds and you must honor their decision."

38
00:03:39.751 --> 00:03:42.585
Amy crossed her arms and pouted.

39
00:03:42.586 --> 00:03:45.636
Smiling at her childish gesture, Laurie said,

40
00:03:45.637 --> 00:03:53.245
"But I promise to visit every day as your messenger, and I'll update you on Beth's condition and other things happening at home."

41
00:03:53.246 --> 00:04:02.872
Amy's eyes brightened and she flashed a big lovely smile, saying, "Oh, would you, Laurie? That would be grand. Thank you so much."

42
00:04:02.873 --> 00:04:10.869
The remainder of the journey was filled with light talk and giggling as the two made an extra effort not to mention Beth's illness.

43
00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:16.753
Amy had been with her family to Aunt March's house several times but had never been there by herself.

44
00:04:16.754 --> 00:04:21.489
She immediately felt intimidated, uncomfortable, and alone.

45
00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:27.717
"Well, at least you're not starving at home, as you seem to have grown since the last time I saw you,"

46
00:04:27.718 --> 00:04:31.542
snapped the old woman, scrutinizing Amy from head to toe.

47
00:04:31.543 --> 00:04:40.494
Aunt March was a critical, difficult, and stubborn person who usually got her way because she was very wealthy and powerful in the community.

48
00:04:40.495 --> 00:04:45.402
However, when it came to her only relative, her nephew Mr. March,

49
00:04:45.403 --> 00:04:52.034
she found that he would not give in to her even though she threatened to withhold any financial help he might need.

50
00:04:52.035 --> 00:04:56.172
Mr. March always kept his ground and never asked her for money.

51
00:04:56.173 --> 00:05:04.492
Even though Aunt March would never admit it, she respected her nephew's sense of values and had a soft spot for her grandnieces.

52
00:05:04.493 --> 00:05:14.977
She loved Jo for her honesty and colorful character, which brought life to her otherwise boring existence, and Amy, for her beauty, good manners, and ambition.

53
00:05:14.978 --> 00:05:20.024
"There are some rules you must obey in this house," Aunt March warned.

54
00:05:20.025 --> 00:05:23.652
"One, you must never shout or raise your voice.

55
00:05:23.653 --> 00:05:26.913
Two, you must never run around the house.

56
00:05:26.914 --> 00:05:34.117
If you break or damage anything, you will pay for it, even if you have to come work for me for the rest of your life.

57
00:05:34.118 --> 00:05:39.958
Three, meals are served at set times. If you are late, then you do not eat.

58
00:05:39.959 --> 00:05:45.554
Four, you will be given chores and expected to complete them by the time given."

59
00:05:45.555 --> 00:05:49.559
"More chores," Amy sighed under her breath.

60
00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:54.224
"What did you say?" Aunt March's sharp ears picked up Amy's mumbling.

61
00:05:54.225 --> 00:05:59.923
"Nothing, Aunt March," muttered Amy, wishing she could calm her shaky legs.

62
00:05:59.924 --> 00:06:05.922
"Five," continued the old woman, "you will sit and read to me every afternoon.

63
00:06:05.923 --> 00:06:10.846
"Your sister used to do that, but she got lazy, then she got sick.

64
00:06:10.847 --> 00:06:14.663
I don't know what to do with that girl. Six . . . "

65
00:06:14.664 --> 00:06:19.422
Amy sighed inwardly and wished she were at home with the others.

66
00:06:19.423 --> 00:06:25.152
Surely, getting sick was not as bad as having to listen to and obey all of Aunt March's rules.

67
00:06:25.153 --> 00:06:31.217
"How am I going to survive?" Amy wondered to herself.

68
00:06:31.218 --> 00:06:39.524
Accepting her plight, Amy decided the only way she was going to manage her stay at Aunt March's was to do exactly as she demanded.

69
00:06:39.525 --> 00:06:47.240
"Don't rub too hard or you might scratch my good silver," Aunt March snapped at Amy, who was polishing endless silver ornaments.

70
00:06:47.241 --> 00:06:50.925
"Careful!" screeched Aunt March's parrot, Polly.

71
00:06:50.926 --> 00:06:56.134
"Yes, ma'am, I'll be very careful," Amy answered dutifully.

72
00:06:56.135 --> 00:07:03.387
While Amy carried on with her chores, Aunt March watched her secretly and thought, "Yes, this one has hope.

73
00:07:03.388 --> 00:07:08.923
She can be useful in society. This one is a lady."

74
00:07:08.924 --> 00:07:12.439
"Careful!" Polly screeched again.

75
00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:18.709
Back home, Dr. Bangs increased the dose of medicine, but Beth's fever still persisted.

76
00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:23.450
Even though Jo felt totally hopeless and useless, she refused to give up.

77
00:07:23.451 --> 00:07:28.644
She continued to do everything she could to take care of Beth in the way she knew best.

78
00:07:28.645 --> 00:07:39.384
And so Jo opened an old book and began reading softly, “A beautiful dream was about to come true for Princess Anastasia . . .”

